{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>לוא</b> — two times in the Masorah, both plene: here and the other: אם לוא יגיד ונשא עונו. To say: I cannot rise before you because of the terafim, but before another I will rise — as we interpret there: אם לו לא יגיד — meaning, to the claimant — ונשא עונו, but to another, if he does not tell, on this account he does not bear his iniquity."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {0 "The bracketed correction [לתובע] replaces the parenthetical (לדיינים) found in the text; both mean 'to the claimant/judge.' The reference 'there' is to the verse cited from the Masorah, identified as Leviticus 5:1."}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:17:30.322336648Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}